WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
1 / Weather → erode → transport → deposit
Weathering loosens rock. Water transports grains downslope; they settle in the basin.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
2 / Bury → compact → cement
Burial packs grains more tightly. Compaction and mineral cement turn sediment into sedimentary rock.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
3 / Metamorphism • change without melting
Heat and directed pressure deform and recrystallize the rock. It remains solid during metamorphism.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
4 / Melt → cool → igneous rock
Melting produces magma; cooling grows interlocking crystals. This is one possible route, not a required rock-cycle loop.
